module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ExtensionByZeroSieveClosure

/-!
# The finitely generated subcomplex spanned by finitely many marked generators, on a site

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `P` be a cochain complex of sheaves of `O`-modules each of
whose terms is presented as a sum of extensions by zero of structure sheaves of slices. Let `W`
be an object and `S` a finite set of marked generators over `W`, closed under the differential
in the sense of
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.ExtensionByZeroSieveClosure`. This file builds **the
subcomplex of `P` spanned by `S`**: in degree `n` it is the image of the morphism

`⊕_{S of degree n} j_{W!}O_W ⟶ P^n`

carrying the tautological generator of each summand to the corresponding marked generator. The
closure hypothesis is exactly what lifts the differential of `P` to the sums of copies of
`j_{W!}O_W`, so the images form a subcomplex; it is a complex of sheaves of modules of finite
type, bounded as soon as `S` is finite, and it contains every section in the span of `S`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.srcObj`: the sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W` indexed by the
  marked generators of a given degree.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.gMap`: the morphism from it to `P^n` sending the
  tautological generators to the marked generators.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.liftMap`: the lift of the differential of `P` to the sums of
  copies of `j_{W!}O_W`, read off the closure hypothesis.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.subcomplex` and
  `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.subcomplexι`: **the subcomplex and its inclusion into `P`.**

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.liftMap_comm`: the lift commutes with the differential.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.subDiff_subDiff`: the induced differential on the images
  squares to zero, because the inclusion of an image is a monomorphism.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.exists_lift_of_inSpan`: **every section over `W` in the span
  of `S` lifts to the subcomplex.** This is what makes the subcomplex contain a prescribed finite
  family of sections.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.epi_factorThruImage_gMap`: each term of the subcomplex is
  generated by finitely many copies of `j_{W!}O_W`.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.isZero_subcomplex_X`: the subcomplex vanishes in every degree
  carrying no generator of `S`, so it is bounded below; it vanishes wherever `P` does, being a
  subobject of `P^n`.
* `Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan.exists_sieve_subcomplex`: **the whole statement** — a covering
  sieve of `V` along whose arrows such a subcomplex contains the restrictions of a prescribed
  finite family of sections of the terms of `P`.

## Implementation notes

**What is *not* here: finite freeness of the restriction.** Over a ringed space the
corresponding construction,
`Stacks.Cohomology.LeftDualPerfect.restrictImageIso`, goes one step further and identifies the
restriction of the degree-`n` term to the open `W` with a finite direct sum of copies of the
structure sheaf, so that the subcomplex is strictly perfect there. **That step is unavailable at
a general site**, for two independent reasons, both of which are automatic for an open of a
space and neither of which follows from anything assumed here.

* `j_W^* j_{W!}O_W ≅ O_W` holds only when `W` is *subterminal*
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.ExtensionByZero.isIso_extensionByZeroAdjunction_unit`, whose hypothesis
  `IsIso (Over.forgetAdjStar W).unit` is discharged for an open of a space by
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.ExtensionByZero.isIso_forgetAdjStar_unit_opens` and by nothing else).
  Without it a copy of `j_{W!}O_W` does not restrict to a copy of the structure sheaf at all.
* Even granted that, `gMap` need not be a monomorphism. Two marked generators with the same index
  and different arrows `W ⟶ U α` name two sections of the *same* summand `j_{U_α!}O_{U_α}`, and
  nothing makes them independent over `O(W)`; over a space `Hom(W, U_α)` has at most one element,
  so distinct marked generators have distinct indices and the independence is the freeness of a
  single tautological generator.

What the subcomplex is, unconditionally, is a bounded complex whose terms are of finite type and
which contains the prescribed sections — which is what the source of [Stacks, Tag 0FPV] asks of
it ("a finitely generated subcomplex"): strict perfection is not claimed there either, the
perfectness of the result coming later, from Tor amplitude and an induction on
pseudo-coherence.

Nothing below is a clause of a tag; these are steps of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FPV], so no
`@[stacks …]` attribute is attached.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPV)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan

attribute [local instance] Abelian.hasFiniteBiproducts

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  (O : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}) (P : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} O) ℤ)
  {I : ℤ → Type u} (U : ∀ n, I n → C) (ιP : ∀ n α, extUnit O (U n α) ⟶ P.X n)

/-- A morphism out of `j_{W!}O_W` is determined by the image of the tautological generator, so
postcomposing it moves that image. -/
theorem fromExtensionByZero_comp {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} O} (W : C) (s : M.val.obj (op W))
    (φ : M ⟶ N) :
    SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero O M W s ≫ φ =
      SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero O N W (φ.val.app (op W) s) :=
  (SheafOfModules.bijective_val_app_gen O N W).1
    ((congrArg (φ.val.app (op W))
        (SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero_val_app_gen O M W s)).trans
      (SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero_val_app_gen O N W _).symm)

variable {W : C} (S : Finset (MarkedT U W))

/-- The sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W` indexed by the marked generators of degree `n` in `S`. -/
abbrev srcObj (n : ℤ) : SheafOfModules.{u} O :=
  ⨁ fun _ : Fin (fibT U S n).card => extUnit O W

/-- The enumeration of the marked generators of degree `n` in `S`. -/
abbrev genIdx (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) : Marked (U n) W :=
  ((fibT U S n).equivFin.symm k).1

/-- The `k`-th enumerated marked generator of degree `n` lies in the fibre of `S` over `n`. -/
theorem genIdx_mem (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) : genIdx U S n k ∈ fibT U S n :=
  ((fibT U S n).equivFin.symm k).2

/-- The section of `srcObj` given by the tautological generator in the summand `k`. -/
abbrev srcGen (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) : (srcObj O U S n).val.obj (op W) :=
  (biproduct.ι (fun _ : Fin (fibT U S n).card => extUnit O W) k).val.app (op W)
    (SheafOfModules.extensionByZeroGen O W)

/-- **The morphism `⊕_{S of degree n} j_{W!}O_W ⟶ P^n`** sending the tautological generator of
each summand to the corresponding marked generator. -/
def gMap (n : ℤ) : srcObj O U S n ⟶ P.X n :=
  biproduct.desc fun k => SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero O (P.X n) W
    (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) (genIdx U S n k))

/-- `gMap` carries the tautological generator of the summand `k` to the `k`-th marked generator. -/
theorem gMap_srcGen (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) :
    (gMap O P U ιP S n).val.app (op W) (srcGen O U S n k) =
      elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) (genIdx U S n k) :=
  (congrArg (fun φ : extUnit O W ⟶ P.X n =>
      φ.val.app (op W) (SheafOfModules.extensionByZeroGen O W))
    (biproduct.ι_desc (fun k => SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero O (P.X n) W
      (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) (genIdx U S n k))) k)).trans
    (SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero_val_app_gen O (P.X n) W _)

/-- `gMap` carries a linear combination of the tautological generators to the same linear
combination of the marked generators of degree `n`. -/
theorem gMap_sum_srcGen (n : ℤ) (a : Marked (U n) W → O.obj.obj (op W)) :
    (gMap O P U ιP S n).val.app (op W)
        (∑ k : Fin (fibT U S n).card, a (genIdx U S n k) • srcGen O U S n k) =
      ∑ m ∈ fibT U S n, a m • elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) m := by
  rw [map_sum, ← Finset.sum_coe_sort (fibT U S n)
      (fun m => a m • elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) m),
    ← (fibT U S n).equivFin.symm.sum_comp]
  refine Fintype.sum_congr _ _ fun k => ?_
  rw [map_smul, gMap_srcGen]

variable {O P U ιP S}

variable (hd : ∀ n, ∀ g ∈ fibT U S n,
  InSpan O (U (n + 1)) (cofanTerm O P U ιP (n + 1)) (fibT U S (n + 1))
    ((P.d n (n + 1)).val.app (op W) (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) g)))

/-- The coefficients expressing the differential of a marked generator in the marked generators
of the next degree. -/
def coefD (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) : Marked (U (n + 1)) W → O.obj.obj (op W) :=
  Classical.choose (hd n (genIdx U S n k) (genIdx_mem U S n k))

/-- The differential of the `k`-th marked generator of degree `n` is the linear combination of the
marked generators of degree `n + 1` with coefficients `coefD hd n k`. -/
theorem coefD_spec (n : ℤ) (k : Fin (fibT U S n).card) :
    (P.d n (n + 1)).val.app (op W)
        (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) (genIdx U S n k)) =
      ∑ m ∈ fibT U S (n + 1), coefD hd n k m •
        elemSec O (U (n + 1)) (cofanTerm O P U ιP (n + 1)) m :=
  Classical.choose_spec (hd n (genIdx U S n k) (genIdx_mem U S n k))

/-- **The lift of the differential of `P` to the sums of copies of `j_{W!}O_W`.** -/
def liftMap (n : ℤ) : srcObj O U S n ⟶ srcObj O U S (n + 1) :=
  biproduct.desc fun k => SheafOfModules.fromExtensionByZero O (srcObj O U S (n + 1)) W
    (∑ l : Fin (fibT U S (n + 1)).card,
      coefD hd n k (genIdx U S (n + 1) l) • srcGen O U S (n + 1) l)

/-- **The lift commutes with the differential of `P`.** -/
theorem liftMap_comm (n : ℤ) :
    liftMap hd n ≫ gMap O P U ιP S (n + 1) = gMap O P U ιP S n ≫ P.d n (n + 1) := by
  refine biproduct.hom_ext' _ _ fun k => ?_
  rw [liftMap, biproduct.ι_desc_assoc, fromExtensionByZero_comp, gMap_sum_srcGen, gMap,
    biproduct.ι_desc_assoc, fromExtensionByZero_comp, coefD_spec]

/-- The differential of the subcomplex spanned by `S`. -/
def subDiff (n : ℤ) : image (gMap O P U ιP S n) ⟶ image (gMap O P U ιP S (n + 1)) :=
  image.map (Arrow.homMk' (liftMap hd n) (P.d n (n + 1)) (liftMap_comm hd n))

/-- The differential of the subcomplex is compatible with the differential of `P` under the
inclusions of the images. -/
theorem subDiff_ι (n : ℤ) :
    subDiff hd n ≫ image.ι (gMap O P U ιP S (n + 1)) =
      image.ι (gMap O P U ιP S n) ≫ P.d n (n + 1) :=
  image.map_homMk'_ι _

/-- The differential of the subcomplex squares to zero. -/
theorem subDiff_subDiff (n : ℤ) : subDiff hd n ≫ subDiff hd (n + 1) = 0 := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (image.ι (gMap O P U ιP S (n + 1 + 1))), Category.assoc, subDiff_ι,
    ← Category.assoc, subDiff_ι, Category.assoc, HomologicalComplex.d_comp_d, comp_zero,
    zero_comp]

/-- **The subcomplex of `P` spanned by the marked generators of `S`**: in degree `n`, the image
of the sum of copies of `j_{W!}O_W` indexed by the generators of `S` of degree `n`. -/
def subcomplex : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} O) ℤ :=
  CochainComplex.of (fun n => image (gMap O P U ιP S n)) (subDiff hd) (subDiff_subDiff hd)

/-- **The inclusion of the subcomplex into `P`.** -/
def subcomplexι : subcomplex hd ⟶ P where
  f n := image.ι (gMap O P U ιP S n)
  comm' i j hij := by
    obtain rfl : i + 1 = j := hij
    exact (subDiff_ι hd i).symm.trans (congrArg (· ≫ image.ι (gMap O P U ιP S (i + 1)))
      (CochainComplex.of_d (fun n => image (gMap O P U ιP S n)) (subDiff hd) i).symm)

/-- The inclusion of the subcomplex into `P` is a monomorphism in each degree. -/
instance mono_subcomplexι_f (n : ℤ) : Mono ((subcomplexι hd).f n) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Mono (image.ι _))

/-- **Every section over `W` in the span of the marked generators of degree `n` lifts to the
subcomplex.** -/
theorem exists_lift_of_inSpan {n : ℤ} {x : (P.X n).val.obj (op W)}
    (hx : InSpan O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) (fibT U S n) x) :
    ∃ y : ((subcomplex hd).X n).val.obj (op W),
      ((subcomplexι hd).f n).val.app (op W) y = x := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hx
  rw [ha, ← gMap_sum_srcGen O P U ιP S n a]
  exact ⟨_, congrArg (fun φ : srcObj O U S n ⟶ P.X n => φ.val.app (op W) _)
    (image.fac (gMap O P U ιP S n))⟩

omit hd in
/-- The sum `srcObj` vanishes in a degree carrying no marked generator of `S`. -/
theorem isZero_srcObj (n : ℤ) (hn : fibT U S n = ∅) : IsZero (srcObj O U S n) := by
  have hcard : (fibT U S n).card = 0 := Finset.card_eq_zero.2 hn
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
  refine biproduct.hom_ext' _ _ fun k => ?_
  exact absurd k.isLt (by omega)

/-- **The subcomplex is bounded**: it vanishes in every degree carrying no generator of `S`,
and `S` is finite. -/
theorem isZero_subcomplex_X (n : ℤ) (hn : fibT U S n = ∅) : IsZero ((subcomplex hd).X n) := by
  have h : IsZero (image (gMap O P U ιP S n)) := by
    rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero, ← cancel_epi (factorThruImage (gMap O P U ιP S n)), comp_zero,
      Category.comp_id]
    exact (isZero_srcObj (O := O) n hn).eq_of_src _ _
  exact h

omit hd in
/-- **Each term of the subcomplex is generated by finitely many copies of `j_{W!}O_W`**: the
factorization of `gMap` through its image is an epimorphism. -/
theorem epi_factorThruImage_gMap (n : ℤ) : Epi (factorThruImage (gMap O P U ιP S n)) :=
  inferInstance

omit hd in
/-- If every marked generator of `S` has degree at least `L`, then `S` has no marked generator in
a degree `n < L`. -/
theorem fibT_eq_empty_of_lt {L : ℤ} (hSL : ∀ x ∈ S, L ≤ x.1) {n : ℤ} (hn : n < L) :
    fibT U S n = ∅ :=
  Finset.eq_empty_of_forall_notMem fun m hm =>
    have hle : L ≤ n := hSL ⟨n, m⟩ (mem_fibT.1 hm)
    absurd hle (by omega)

variable (O P U ιP)

/-- **The finitely generated bounded subcomplex of `P` containing a prescribed finite family of
sections, on a site.** Let `P` be a complex of sheaves of `O`-modules whose terms are presented
as sums of extensions by zero of structure sheaves of slices, with `P^n = 0` for `n > b`, and
let finitely many sections of the terms of `P`, in degrees `≥ L`, over an object `V` be given.
Then along the arrows `f : W ⟶ V` of a covering sieve of `V` there is a finite set `S` of marked
generators over `W`, closed under the differential, such that the subcomplex of `P` it spans
contains the restrictions of the given sections. That subcomplex is bounded — it vanishes below
`L` by `fibT_eq_empty_of_lt` and `isZero_subcomplex_X`, and above `b` as a subobject of `P` —
its inclusion into `P` is a degreewise monomorphism by
`mono_subcomplexι_f`, and each of its terms is, by construction, the image of a finite sum of
copies of `j_{W!}O_W`. -/
theorem exists_sieve_subcomplex (hc : ∀ n, IsColimit (cofanTerm O P U ιP n)) (b L : ℤ)
    (hb : ∀ n, b < n → IsZero (P.X n)) {V : C} {κ : Type*} [Finite κ] (deg : κ → ℤ)
    (s : ∀ i, (P.X (deg i)).val.obj (op V)) (hL : ∀ i, L ≤ deg i) :
    ∃ R : Sieve V, R ∈ J V ∧ ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (f : W ⟶ V), R.arrows f →
      ∃ (S : Finset (MarkedT U W)) (hd : ∀ n, ∀ g ∈ fibT U S n,
          InSpan O (U (n + 1)) (cofanTerm O P U ιP (n + 1)) (fibT U S (n + 1))
            ((P.d n (n + 1)).val.app (op W) (elemSec O (U n) (cofanTerm O P U ιP n) g))),
        (∀ x ∈ S, L ≤ x.1) ∧
        ∀ i, ∃ y : ((subcomplex hd).X (deg i)).val.obj (op W),
          ((subcomplexι hd).f (deg i)).val.app (op W) y =
            (P.X (deg i)).val.map f.op (s i) := by
  obtain ⟨R, hR, hRspec⟩ := exists_sieve_closedSpan O P U ιP hc b L hb deg s hL
  refine ⟨R, hR, fun W f hf => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨S, hSL, hsec, hd⟩ := hRspec f hf
  exact ⟨S, hd, hSL, fun i => exists_lift_of_inSpan hd (hsec i)⟩

end Stacks.Sites.ExtensionByZeroSpan

end
